{"key":"enterprise/T1136.002","id":"T1136.002","name":"Domain Account","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1136","tactics":["persistence"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may create a domain account to maintain access to victim systems. Domain accounts are those managed by Active Directory Domain Services where access and permissions are configured across systems and services that are part of that domain. Domain accounts can cover user, administrator, and service accounts. With a sufficient level of access, the net user /add /domain command can be used to create a domain account. Such accounts may be…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1136/002","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--7610cada-1499-41a4-b3dd-46467b68d177","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:57.883Z","source_object_version":"1.1","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0067","name":"Logon Session Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0067","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9ce98c86-8d30-4043-ba54-0784d478d0b5","page":"telemetry/DC0067/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0002","name":"User Account Authentication","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0002","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a953ca55-921a-44f7-9b8d-3d40141aa17e","page":"telemetry/DC0002/"},{"id":"DC0014","name":"User Account Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0014","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--deb22295-7e37-4a3b-ac6f-c86666fbe63d","page":"telemetry/DC0014/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0003","name":"T1136.002 Detection Strategy - Domain Account Creation Across Platforms","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0003","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--aae40136-73f7-45e8-a37f-104ae7155bbe","relationship_id":"relationship--140e6844-f9bb-4e31-bb57-370d1fd830f3"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0006","name":"Analytic 0006","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0003#AN0006","guidance":"Adversary uses built-in tools such as 'net user /add /domain' or PowerShell to create a domain user account. The behavior chain includes: (1) suspicious process execution on a domain controller followed by (2) user account creation event (Event ID 4720) on the same host.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0003"},{"id":"AN0007","name":"Analytic 0007","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0003#AN0007","guidance":"Adversary with access to domain management tools (e.g., `realmd`, `samba-tool`, `ldapmodify`) creates a new domain user via command-line utilities. Behavior chain: LDAP command or script triggers → user entry added in AD via Kerberos/LDAP traffic.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0003"},{"id":"AN0008","name":"Analytic 0008","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0003#AN0008","guidance":"macOS clients joined to AD via LDAP may script account provisioning via `dsconfigad`, `dscl`, or LDAP scripts. Detection occurs when such tools run on a domain-joined system, followed by authentication attempts by a previously unseen account.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0003"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0014","component":"User Account Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Security","channel":"EventCode=4720","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0006","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0003#AN0006","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0014/"},{"component_